WHAT: Relaxed the speed-mode inliner limits for multi-use small functions.
Increased max_multi_use_inlinee_blocks from 1 to 3, max_multi_use_inlinee_insts
from 6 to 12.

WHY: ABI decoder bounds-check helper functions weren't being inlined because
they're called from multiple sites. These are small (1-2 blocks) but the
strict multi-use limit prevented inlining. Once inlined, constant propagation
can eliminate trivially-dead bounds checks.

GAS IMPACT: -462 gas total across affected contracts.
  erc20/transfer: -92, erc20/approve: -46
  governance: -21 to -46 across 6 functions
  amm/addLiquidity: -77

CODEGEN IMPACT: More compact PUSH instructions, eliminated jumps. Even with
slightly more total opcodes, the eliminated function call overhead and
subsequent constant folding produce smaller runtime gas.

TEAM NOTES: This is the first of several inliner tuning commits. The pattern
is: relax inliner limits → more functions get inlined → downstream passes
(constant prop, dead code elimination) can clean up what was previously
hidden behind call boundaries. The inliner is the gatekeeper for most
other optimizations.

CROSS-CUTTING: Helped erc20, amm, and governance despite targeting ABI
decoder helpers. Any contract that decodes calldata benefits.
